SPRINT — this week

File: openOODA/SPRINT.oot
What to do next. DESIGN is the want. SHIPPED is what exists. PM is the pin.

Handoff
  Read RULES.oot. Then SHIPPED.oot and PM.oot.
  Proof is `oodac check oodac/main.oo` or emit + gcc + run.
  Rebuild from ooda/:
    bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac

Pin
  Release v0.198.0-alpha (Heading to v0.200.0-beta)
  Live check (this machine): OK in about 25 seconds, about 0.32 GiB RAM.
  Rebuild: bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build

Open (Road to Beta — Phase 2)

  Track 1: Compiler & Code Generation Floor
  [ ] RTB-6: Pure .wasm binary bytecode emission (upgrade from .wat to \0asm).
  [ ] RTB-7: Self-host compiler check performance (<10s check & memory optimization).
  [ ] RTB-8: LLVM self-hosting expansion (struct matching & full self-host parity).

  Track 2: Security, Sandboxing & OS Containment
  [ ] RTB-9: Linux Kernel Landlock sandboxing (filesystem path jails under &FsCap).
  [ ] RTB-10: POSIX heap rlimits & memory quotas (setrlimit under &MemCap).
  [ ] RTB-11: Fine-grained struct field secret taint tracking.

  Track 3: Developer Ecosystem & Tooling
  [ ] RTB-12: Pure self-hosted language server (ooda lsp native JSON-RPC server).
  [ ] RTB-13: Multi-error in-place code fixer (ooda fix auto-patching E_CAP & imports).
  [ ] RTB-14: Package registry & cryptographic lockfile resolver (pm install/add).

  Track 4: Standard Library Expansion
  [ ] RTB-15: Buffered filesystem stream API (std/fs/file.oo & std/fs/path.oo).
  [ ] RTB-16: Cryptographic hashing & encoding (std/crypto/sha256.oo & base64.oo).
  [ ] RTB-17: Text processing & regular expressions (std/text/regex.oo).

Later (do not start yet)
  Moonshots in MOONSHOTS.oot (Auto binary transmutation, Merkle undo-RAM, ZK execution, AST macros, SoA layout).

Closed (Delivered in v0.198.0-alpha)
  [x] Compiler self-hosting: check of all 177 modules passes OK.
  [x] Native C & LLVM emit: ooda run, spawn, secret sinks, LLVM hello.
  [x] RTB-1: Essential collections & formats (std/hash/map.oo & std/markup/json.oo).
  [x] RTB-2: I/O & networking floor (std/time/chrono.oo & std/net/http.oo).
  [x] RTB-3: CLI developer workflow (cli/cli_init.oo, cli/cli_doc.oo, init/test/doc).
  [x] RTB-4: Rich compiler diagnostics (cli/diag_fmt.oo with caret pointers ^^^^).
  [x] RTB-5: Concurrency & synchronization (std/sync/channel.oo bounded message queues).
